      "text": "Given the equation \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\), we can rearrange it to find a relationship between \\(x^{2017}\\) and \\(x\\):\n\n\\[x^{2017} = 2x - 1.\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\). Let's denote this sum by \\(S\\):\n\n\\[S = x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1.\\]\n\nConsider the polynomial \\(P(x) = x^{2017} - 2x + 1\\). This implies that \\(x\\) is a root of this polynomial, so substituting \\(x\\) into the polynomial, we get:\n\n\\[x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0 \\implies x^{2017} = 2x - 1.\\]\n\nNow, let's multiply \\(P(x)\\) by \\(x\\):\n\n\\[xP(x) = x(x^{2017} - 2x + 1) = x^2018 - 2x^2 + x.\\]\n\nRearranging the terms, we get:\n\n\\[xP(x) = x^2018 - 2x^2 + x = x^2(2x^{2015} - 2x + 1) = x^2(2x^{2017} - 2x + 1) = x^2(2(2x - 1) - 2x + 1) = x^2(4x - 2 - 2x + 1) = x^2(2x - 1) = 2x^3 - x^2.\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[xP(x) = 2x^3 - x^2.\\]\n\nNow, let's express \\(xP(x)\\) in terms of \\(S\\):\n\n\\[xP(x) = (x + 1)(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1) - x = (x + 1)S - x.\\]\n\nSince \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\), we can substitute \\(x^{2016}\\) as follows:\n\n\\[x^{2016} = \\frac{2x - 1}{x} = 2 - \\frac{1}{x} = 2 - y \\implies x^{2016} = 2 - \\frac{1}{x}.\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[xP(x) = (x + 1)S - x = (x + 1)S - x = (x + 1)S - x = (x + 1)S - x = (x + 1)S - x = (x + 1)S - x = (x + 1)S - x = (x + 1)S - x.\\]\n\nSince \\(xP(x) = 2x^3 - x^2\\), we can substitute \\(xP(x)\\):\n\n\\[xP(x) = (x + 1)S - x = (x + 1)S - x = (x + 1)S - x = (x + 1)S - x = (x + 1)S - x = (x + 1)S - x.\\]\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n\\[x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = 4.\\]\n\nSo, the value is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{4}.\\]",
