      "text": "Given the equation \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\), we can rearrange it to express \\(x^{2017}\\) in terms of \\(x\\):\n\n\\[x^{2017} = 2x - 1.\\]\n\nWe are asked to find the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\). Notice that this is a geometric series with the first term \\(1\\) (when \\(x = 1\\)) and common ratio \\(x\\). The sum of the first 2017 terms of this geometric series is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x^{2017} - 1}{x - 1}.\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\) into the sum formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(2x - 1) - 1}{x - 1} = \\frac{2x - 2}{x - 1} = \\frac{2(x - 1)}{x - 1} = 2.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
