      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given the equation \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\), we need to find the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\).\n\nFirst, let's denote the sum we need to find by \\(S\\):\n\\[\nS = x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\n\\]\n\nWe can express \\(S\\) in a telescoping form. Notice that:\n\\[\nS = \\frac{x^{2017} - 1}{x - 1}\n\\]\nThis is derived from the geometric series sum formula \\(1 + x + x^2 + \\dots + x^{2016} = \\frac{x^{2017} - 1}{x - 1}\\).\n\nFrom the given equation \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\), we can rearrange it to:\n\\[\nx^{2017} = 2x - 1\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\) into the expression for \\(S\\), we get:\n\\[\nS = \\frac{2x - 1 - 1}{x - 1} = \\frac{2x - 2}{x - 1} = \\frac{2(x - 1)}{x - 1} = 2\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
